n      <!-- brim -->\n      <path d=\"M205 278 Q 300 258 395 278 Q 300 296 205 278 Z\" fill=\"#e8b96a\" stroke=\"#b9822e\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n      <!-- brim decorative band -->\n      <path d=\"M228 277 Q 300 262 372 277 Q 300 291 228 277 Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e74c3c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n      <!-- crown -->\n      <path d=\"M258 272 L 266 240 Q 300 224 334 240 L 342 272 Q 300 284 258 272 Z\" fill=\"#fdf6e3\" stroke=\"#b9822e\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n      <!-- crown band -->\n      <path d=\"M262 266 Q 300 278 338 266 L 336 258 Q 300 270 264 258 Z\" fill=\"#e74c3c\"/>\n      <!-- small rosette -->\n      <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"244\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#3f7fbf\"/>\n    </g>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- Splash around board -->\n  <g fill=\"#ffffff\" opacity=\"0.85\">\n    <circle cx=\"165\" cy=\"445\" r=\"8\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"438\" r=\"5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"440\" cy=\"445\" r=\"8\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"455\" cy=\"438\" r=\"5\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"185\" cy=\"452\" r=\"4\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"420\" cy=\"452\" r=\"4\"/>\n  </g>\n\n  <!-- Splash arcs -->\n  <path d=\"M155 448 Q 140 430 148 415\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n  <path d=\"M450 448 Q 465 430 457 415\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#ffffff\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n</svg>\n```\n\nA penguin in a classic striped sombrero rides a red-and-white e-foil, gliding above the water with its hydrofoil wing and propeller submerged, complete with splashes and bubbles. Just save it as a `.svg` file and open it in any browser!",
    "reasoning_content": "The user wants an SVG of a penguin wearing a sombrero, riding an e-foil. Let me create a fun, detailed SVG.\n\nElements:\n- Water (blue waves)\n- E-foil: board, mast, hydrofoil wing underwater, small propeller\n- Penguin: black body, white belly, orange beak and feet, eyes\n- Sombrero: wide brim, tall crown, colorful pattern\n- Maybe some splashes\n\nLet me construct the coordinates. Canvas is 600x600.\n\nWater surface at y ~ 450. Board is above the water surface, hydrofoil is underwater.\n\nBoard: x 180 to 420, y ~ 430-445, rounded shape. Mast rises from the center of the board to the deck. Propeller at the back of the board.\n\nPenguin stands on the board: body ellipse, feet on the board, flippers, head, beak.\n\nSombrero on top of the head: wide elliptical brim, crown.\n\nUnderwater: vertical mast extends down from the board to the hydrofoil wing (T-shape) at y ~ 520.\n\nLet me write the SVG code.\n\nPenguin: body center x=300. Board top at y=432. Feet at y~428. Body from y~330 to 430. Head circle at y~300. Top of head ~270. Sombrero brim at y~275, crown above that.\n\nLet me draw:\n\nWater: rect y=450 to 600, blue, some wave paths.\n\nBoard: path around (170,430) to (430,430), slightly curved. Use a path with a curve: M170 435 Q300 420 430 435 L425 448 Q300 438 175 448 Z. Color is white/red.\n\nMast: rect x=296 y=435 width=8 height=15 (visible above water surface). Propeller: small circle + blades at the rear x~410.\n\nHydrofoil underwater: vertical strut rect x=297 y=450 height=80; wing: horizontal ellipse/shape at y=535, x 240-360; front small canard at y=505, x 270-330.\n\nPenguin body:\n- Feet: orange ellipses at (270,430) and (330,430) \u2014 actually should be on the board so y~428.\n- Body: ellipse cx=300 cy=385 rx=55 ry=70 fill black.\n- White belly: ellipse cx=300 cy=395 rx=38 ry=55 white.\n- Head: circle cx=300 cy=310 r=38 black. Connect to body \u2014 the overlap is fine.\n- White face/cheeks: small arcs optional.\n- Eyes: white circle cx=285/315 cy=305 r=8, pupils r=4.\n- Beak: orange triangle at (300, 318): path M288 318 L312 318 L300 332 Z.\n- Flippers: left path curving outward, right similarly.\n- Sombrero: brim as a large ellipse cx=300 cy=278 rx=85 ry=14; crown: path M255 278 L262 245 Q300 230 338 245 L345 278 Z; band stripe; decorative stripes. Top of head at y~272, so brim at 278 works.\n\nSombrero colors: brim in tan #e8b96a, crown in white/cream, red band, decorative band.\n\nSplash: some white circles near the waterline at the edges of the board.\n\nWaves: wavy line at y=450.\n\nAdd a sun? Keep it simple. Add a few water droplets.\n\nLet me write the final SVG."
